      "text": "To find the ratio of the volume of a cube with edge length six inches to the volume of a cube with edge length one foot, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the volume of the first cube with edge length six inches.\n2. Calculate the volume of the second cube with edge length one foot.\n3. Find the ratio of the volumes.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the volume of the first cube.**\n\nThe volume \\( V_1 \\) of a cube with edge length \\( s \\) is given by:\n\\[ V_1 = s^3 \\]\n\nFor the first cube, the edge length \\( s = 6 \\) inches:\n\\[ V_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the volume of the second cube.**\n\nFor the second cube, the edge length \\( s = 1 \\) foot. Since 1 foot is equal to 12 inches, the edge length in inches is 12 inches:\n\\[ V_2 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\n**Step 3: Find the ratio of the volumes.**\n\nThe ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube is:\n\\[ \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{1728} \\]\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 1728. The GCD of 216 and 1728 is 216. Therefore, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by 216:\n\\[ \\frac{216}{1728} = \\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8} \\]\n\nThus, the ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}} \\]",
